From 26ecf14f6d22a2064cd9da97a04ac1030268b786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 07:45:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix "Finish setting up" screen blocking phone sign-in

The setup screen appeared because the server had no Firebase web config,
but its wording ("enable Phone sign-in...") suggested the Phone provider
was the problem, so enabling it and adding test numbers didn't help.

- Accept the Firebase web config pasted into src/config/firebase.ts (the
  console snippet as-is), or as one FIREBASE_WEB_CONFIG variable, in
  addition to the individual FIREBASE_* variables
- Detect obviously wrong configs, including the invalid API key and app
  ID from the original code, and warn on the sign-in screen
- Rewrite the setup screen as a numbered checklist that explains the
  config is what's missing and shows the exact domain to authorize
- Sign-in errors now name the Firebase project and domain in use and
  cover more codes (auth not initialised, API key restrictions)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MyCre331b5gFD1kCpkyBL6
